codex
The edge probes found no released loss of a consensus elision and no real mark edit hidden by alias accounting. They also reproduced an existing quote behavior: without detector quote evidence, both SF4 and SF5 remove a leading opening quote. I’ll record that as an out-of-scope note. The reported 26→1 count is confirmed as effective-label omissions; the remaining one is already missing from Google on a held line.
